# gh-app-shim configuration.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/gh-app-shim/config.env and fill it in.
# It is sourced by bin/gh, so keep it shell-safe: KEY=value, no spaces around =.
# NEVER commit the real config.env or the .pem key — only this example belongs in git.

# --- GitHub App identity (not secret; the private key is the only secret) ---
# Replace these with your own App's values: the "App ID" from the App's settings
# page, and the numeric installation id from its installation settings URL.
APP_ID=123456
INSTALLATION_ID=12345678

# --- Private key (.pem) for the App. Keep it chmod 600, outside the repo. ----
KEY_PATH=$HOME/.config/gh-app-shim/app.pem

# --- Path to the real gh binary. install.sh sets this automatically. ---------
# Leave commented to auto-detect from PATH (only works if a non-shim gh exists).
# REAL_GH=$HOME/.local/share/gh-app-shim/gh

# --- Optional: where to cache the hourly installation token. -----------------
# TOKEN_CACHE=/tmp/gh-app-shim-token

# --- Optional: orgs/repos where the bot should act as YOU, not the App. ------
# By default a Claude Code session acts as the App bot. For repos/orgs listed
# here, the shim instead passes through to the real gh with your own auth — so
# Claude acts as you there. Whether the bot can touch a repo at all is governed
# by the App's GitHub permissions; this only chooses which credential is used.
#
# Space-separated, case-insensitive. Orgs match the owner; repos are
# "owner/repo". Both unset by default → every Claude Code call acts as the bot.
# Commands with no detectable repo (e.g. `gh api user`) act as the bot. The
# target repo is taken from an explicit -R/--repo flag, else the cwd's git
# origin/upstream remote.
#
# PASSTHROUGH_ORGS="my-personal-org"
# PASSTHROUGH_REPOS="me/dotfiles"

# --- Optional: second GitHub App for the `gh-claude-reviewer` command. -------
# `gh-claude` always acts as the App above; `gh-claude-reviewer` always acts as
# the App below. Both ignore the session marker and the passthrough lists — the
# command name is the choice of identity. Set these only if you use a second
# bot; without them `gh-claude-reviewer` stops with an error and `gh` /
# `gh-claude` are unaffected.
#
# REVIEWER_APP_ID=234567
# REVIEWER_INSTALLATION_ID=23456789
# REVIEWER_KEY_PATH=$HOME/.config/gh-app-shim/reviewer.pem
